      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "JERRY LOUIE (1) turned in a moderate effort last time when sixth at this track over 340m behind Otto Rhode (20.15) in a Grade 5. Scored at his previous run. Better than the latest run and deserves another chance. TOWELLED UP (6) has some solid form under his belt and proved too classy last time to win by a nose at this track in a handy 19.64 beating SHE'S TROUBLE. Remains without a win from the draw but has been in the placings two times from three attempts. Leading chance again. GREEDY BUTCHER (7) doesn't have the best strike-rate but recent form is sound. Has been in the money the last three starts, the latest when third (30.39) at Launceston. Has a good record here at this journey. Remains without a win from the draw but has been in the placings five times from seven attempts. Overdue and is among the main hopes. PACK LEADER (2) should be thereabouts despite an unplaced run here most recently.",
